## Story Description
frontend/src/pages/dashboard/SupplierPage.tsx fetches all suppliers at line 75 with no limit param, so the server default of 50 applies. Engagements with more than 50 suppliers only show 50 in the table — the rest are silently missing with no indication to the user. The fix is to add { limit: 500 } to the API call params. The backend by-supplier endpoint accepts limit up to le=1000, so 500 is within bounds. Full server-side pagination with load-more is out of scope for this sprint.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: frontend/src/pages/dashboard/SupplierPage.tsx — on line 75, change 'api.get(`/api/engagements/${engagementId}/cube/by-supplier`)' to 'api.get(`/api/engagements/${engagementId}/cube/by-supplier`, { params: { limit: 500 } })' so the full list is fetched
- Run: cd frontend && npm run build — TypeScript build must succeed with no errors
- Verify: the queryFn on line 74-76 in SupplierPage.tsx now includes { params: { limit: 500 } } in the axios call

